The error you're encountering is due to the fact that the result from the OpenAI API is not a string but an object. When you try to call `String.prototype.trim` on an object, it throws an error because `trim` expects a string. Instead, you should convert the object to a string using `String(JSON.stringify(obj))` or similar methods.

However, the more robust approach is to avoid using the `trim()` method altogether, as it's unnecessary when dealing with JSON. JSON is already well-structured and doesn't require trimming. Instead, you can handle the error more gracefully

